[32m+[m[32m## 1. Overview[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAnime platforms contain thousands of titles with varying ratings, audience sizes, and engagement metrics. This project turns anime metadata into a structured REST API for querying the dataset and exploring statistical patterns.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe application separates HTTP handling, business logic, data access, preprocessing, and analytical functions. It includes automated tests, configuration management, technical documentation, and a GitHub Actions continuous integration workflow.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Key features[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Search, filter, sort, and paginate anime records.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Retrieve individual anime using MyAnimeList IDs.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Calculate dataset summaries and data-quality statistics.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Rank anime using supported numerical metrics.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Compare genres and anime types.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Analyze completion, drop, and favorite rates.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Examine metric distributions, percentiles, skewness, and kurtosis.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Analyze metric concentration through Pareto/decile grouping.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Validate requests and return structured error responses.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Run automated tests and code-quality checks.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Browse detailed technical documentation using MkDocs Material.[m
